pentelemetry-go-7474.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875d9f208a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7474.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7474.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 32141, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:06\", \"token_count\": 11686, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-06]\\n\\n# Pull Request: Use sync.Map and atomics for fixed bucket histograms (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go#7474)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7474  \\n\\n**Author**: dashpole  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-08T14:31:21Z · **Updated**: 2025-12-11T16:56:31Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: merged (2025-12-11T16:56:04Z)  \\n\\n**Branch**: `optimize_syncmap_histogram` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +560 / -201 across 7 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: v1.40.0\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nImplement a lockless histogram using atomics, and use a sync.Map for attribute access.  This improves performance by ~2x.\\n\\nThe design is very similar to https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7427, but with one additional change to make the histogram data point itself atomic:\\n\\n* For cumulative histograms, which do not use a hot/cold limitedSyncMap, we use a hot/cold data point.  This way, we maintain the keys in the sync map, but still ensure that collection gets a consistent view of measure() calls.\\n\\nParallel benchmarks:\\n\\n```\\n\\n                                                                       │  main.txt   │              hist.txt              │\\n\\n                                                                       │   sec/op    │   sec/op     vs base               │\\n\\nSyncMeasure/NoView/ExemplarsDisabled/Int64Histogram/Attributes/10-24     274.5n ± 2%   125.2n ± 5%  -54.42% (p=0.002 n=6)\\n\\nSyncMeasure/NoView/ExemplarsDisabled/Float64Histogram/Attributes/10-24   274.1n ± 2%   132.5n ± 2%  -51.65% (p=0.002 n=6)\\n\\ngeomean                                                                  274.3n        128.8n       -53.05%\\n\\n```\\n\\nzero memory allocations before and after this change for Measure().  Omitted for brevity\\n\\nBenchmarks for collect:\\n\\n```\\n\\n                                                    │   main.txt    │               hist.txt               │\\n\\n                                                    │    sec/op     │    sec/op     vs base                │\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src pr 06 pull request use sync map and atom for fix bucket histogram open telemetri opentelemetri go 7474 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7474 author dashpol creat 2025 10 08t14 31 21z updat 2025 12 11t16 56 31z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state merg 2025 12 11t16 56 04z branch optim _ syncmap _ histogram main chang 560 201 across 7 file label mileston v1 400 descript implement a lockless histogram use atom and use a sync map for attribut access this improv perform by 2x the design is veri similar to http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7427 but with one addit chang to make the histogram data point itself atom for cumul histogram which do not use a hot cold limitedsyncmap we use a hot cold data point this way we maintain the key in the sync map but still ensur that collect get a consist view of measur call parallel benchmark main txt hist txt sec op sec op v base syncmeasur noview exemplarsdis int64histogram attribut 1024 274 5n 2 125 2n 5 54 42 p 0 002 n 6 syncmeasur noview exemplarsdis float64histogram attribut 1024 274 1n 2 132 5n 2 51 65 p 0 002 n 6 geomean 274 3n 128 8n 53 05 zero memori alloc befor and after this chang for measur omit for breviti benchmark for collect main txt hist txt sec op sec op v base\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875d9f208a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7474.md\", \"id\": \"432d9a43e09b0cb1\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33901138810178694, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1387887087168385, \"vector_similarity\": 0.80619764, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7474.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875d9f208a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7474.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7474.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 32141, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:06\", \"token_count\": 11686, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**dashpole** — COMMENTED — 2025-11-12T14:59:04Z\\n\\n**MrAlias** — APPROVED — 2025-12-04T17:44:24Z\\n\\n**dmathieu** — APPROVED — 2025-12-09T14:41:46Z\\n\\n**dashpole** — COMMENTED — 2025-12-09T16:07:17Z\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-06]\\n\\n# Pull Request: Use sync.Map and atomics for fixed bucket histograms (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go#7474)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7474  \\n\\n**Author**: dashpole  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-08T14:31:21Z · **Updated**: 2025-12-11T16:56:31Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: merged (2025-12-11T16:56:04Z)  \\n\\n**Branch**: `optimize_syncmap_histogram` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +560 / -201 across 7 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: v1.40.0\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Review Comments (44)\\n\\n**MrAlias** on `sdk/metric/internal/aggregate/atomic.go` — 2025-10-08T22:16:25Z\\n\\nThere are data-races here because these are all stored as 3 separate fields.\\n\\nWhat about something like this instead?\\n\\n```go\\n\\n// extrema holds the minimum and maximum of a set of values.\\n\\ntype extrema[N int64 | float64] struct {\\n\\n\\tmin, max N\\n\\n\\tset      bool\\n\\n}\\n\\nfunc newExtrema[N int64 | float64](minimum, maximum N) extrema[N] {\\n\\n\\treturn extrema[N]{min: minimum, max: maximum, set: true}\\n\\n}\\n\\n// update updates the extrema with the provided value.\\n\\n//\\n\\n// If the current extrema already contains a minimum less than or equal to val,\\n\\n// no update to minimum is made.\\n\\n//\\n\\n// If the current extrema already contains a maximum greater than or equal to\\n\\n// val, no update to maximum is made.\\n\\nfunc (e extrema[N]) update(val N) extrema[N] {\\n\\n\\tif !e.set {\\n\\n\\t\\te.min = val\\n\\n\\t\\te.max = val\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"dashpol comment 2025 11 12t14 59 04z mralia approv 2025 12 04t17 44 24z dmathieu approv 2025 12 09t14 41 46z dashpol comment 2025 12 09t16 07 17z sourc id src pr 06 pull request use sync map and atom for fix bucket histogram open telemetri opentelemetri go 7474 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7474 author dashpol creat 2025 10 08t14 31 21z updat 2025 12 11t16 56 31z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state merg 2025 12 11t16 56 04z branch optim _ syncmap _ histogram main chang 560 201 across 7 file label mileston v1 400 review comment 44 mralia on sdk metric intern aggreg atom go 2025 10 08t22 16 25z there are data race here becaus these are all store a 3 separ field what about someth like this instead go extremum hold the minimum and maximum of a set of valu type extremum n int64 float64 struct min max n set bool func newextrema n int64 float64 minimum maximum n extremum n return extremum n min minimum max maximum set true updat updat the extremum with the provid valu if the current extremum alreadi contain a minimum less than or equal to val no updat to minimum is made if the current extremum alreadi contain a maximum greater than or equal to val no updat to maximum is made func e extremum n updat val n extremum n if e set e min val e max val\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875d9f208a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7474.md\", \"id\": \"a3246858fc4bc1e2\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33177861610178694, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1387887087168385, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7820884, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7474.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875d9f208a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7474.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7474.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 32141, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:06\", \"token_count\": 11686, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- Improve performance of histogram `Record` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric` when min and max are disabled using `NoMinMax`. (#7306)\\n\\n- Improve error handling for dropped data during translation by using `prometheus.NewInvalidMetric` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/prometheus`. ⚠️ **Breaking Change:** Previously, these cases were only logged and scrapes succeeded. Now, when translation would drop data (e.g., invalid label/value), the exporter emits a `NewInvalidMetric`, and Prometheus scrapes **fail with HTTP 500** by default. To preserve the prior behavior (scrapes succeed while errors are logged), configure your Prometheus HTTP handler with: `promhttp.HandlerOpts{ ErrorHandling: promhttp.ContinueOnError }`. (#7363)\\n\\n- Replace fnv hash with xxhash in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/attribute` for better performance. (#7371)\\n\\n- The default `TranslationStrategy` in `go.opentelemetry.io/exporters/prometheus` is changed from `otlptranslator.NoUTF8EscapingWithSuffixes` to `otlptranslator.UnderscoreEscapingWithSuffixes`. (#7421)\\n\\n- Improve performance of concurrent measurements in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric`. (#7427)\\n\\n- Include W3C TraceFlags (bits 0–7) in the OTLP `Span.Flags` field in `go.opentelemetry.io/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/otlptracehttp` and `go.opentelemetry.io/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/otlptracegrpc`. (#7438)\\n\\n- The `ErrorType` function in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/semconv/v1.37.0` now handles custom error types.\\n\\n  If an error implements an `ErrorType() string` method, the return value of that method will be used as the error type. (#7442)\\n\\n### Fixed\\n\\n- Fix `WithInstrumentationAttributes` options in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace`, `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/metric`, and `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/log` to properly merge attributes when passed multiple times instead of replacing them. Attributes with duplicate keys will use the last value passed. (#7300)\\n\\n- The equality of `attribute.Set` when using the `Equal` method is not affected by the user overriding the empty set pointed to by `attribute.EmptySet` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/attribute`. (#7357)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"improv perform of histogram record in go opentelemetri io otel sdk metric when min and max are disabl use nominmax 7306 improv error handl for drop data dure translat by use prometheus newinvalidmetr in go opentelemetri io otel export prometheus break chang previous these case were onli log and scrape succeed now when translat would drop data e g invalid label valu the export emit a newinvalidmetr and prometheus scrape fail with http 500 by default to preserv the prior behavior scrape succeed while error are log configur your prometheus